## Summary

The contract test is a powerful testing methodology that allows developers to specify the behavior of the system under test using assertions or postconditions in the form of constraints. In this case, contracts were established for the `IndexOf` method, validating that it returns the correct value given specific pre-conditions.

There are several benefits in implementing contract tests as they provide high assurance that the system behaves as expected, and they also provide an automatic verification of the behavior without needing to execute other test cases.

However, keep in mind that these types of tests are best suited for complex systems, where the system behavior cannot be easily validated using traditional unit tests.--------------------
            Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret >= 0 && New_Ret <= New_arrListCount);
        }
    }
